 75SE    76SE(P,D):XUNDL-2             2007SCZX,2008SC03                  200803
 75SE c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2007ScZX: private communication    
 75SE2c  from J. P. Schiffer, Argonne National Lab, Oct 27, 2007; and           
 75SE3c  2008Sc03: Phys Rev Lett 100, 112501 (2008).                            
 75SE c  2007ScZX contains data details for fourteen different                  
 75SE4c  reactions, results of which are summarized and used in 2008Sc03        
 75SE c  Compiled by S. Geraedts and B. Singh (McMaster): Nov 5, 2007.          
 75SE2c  Edited by B. Singh, March 27, 2008                                     
 75SE c  E=23 MeV beam provided by Yale tandem accelerator. Enriched            
 75SE2c  target. Particles detected with Enge spectrograph and gas-filled focal 
 75SE3c  plane detector backed by a scintillator. Measured cross sections.      
 75SE4c  FWHM=40 keV. Spectroscopic factors deduced from analysis of cross      
 75SE5c  section data by DWBA calculations using PTOLEMY code.                  
 75SE c  The experiments were designed to determine occupation of valence       
 75SE2c  neutron orbitals in the ground states of {+76}Ge and {+76}Se by        
 75SE3c  precise measurements of cross sections through particle-transfer       
 75SE4c  reactions. Cross sections were measured at angles where these are      
 75SE5c  maximum.                                                               
 75SE c  Single-particle transfer reactions studied in 2008Sc03, 2007ScZX:      
 75SE2c  {+74}Ge(d,p); {+76}Ge(d,p); {+76}Ge(p,d); {+76}Se(d,p); {+76}Se(p,d);  
 75SE3c  {+78}Se(d,p); {+74}Ge({+3}He,|a); {+74}Ge(|a,{+3}He);                  
 75SE4c  {+76}Ge({+3}He,|a); {+76}Ge(|a,{+3}He); {+76}Se({+3}He,|a);            
 75SE5c  {+76}Se(|a,{+3}He); {+78}Se({+3}He,|a); {+78}Se(|a,{+3}He). See        
 75SExc  relevant dataset for each reaction.                                    
 75SE c  Uncertainty in cross sections: statistical uncertainty of 1%           
 75SE2c  for strong peaks; systematic uncertainties of 5% in absolute values    
 75SE3c  and 3% in relative values.                                             
 75SE c  All data listed here are from 2007ScZX                                 
